129
# Parse failures under `bash scripts/verify-documented-flags.sh --execute`,
# which RUNS each command in a throwaway directory instead of appending --help.
# Down-only. Read by the weekly `documented-flags-deep` CI job.
#
# Measured 2026-08-25 against pmat 3.32.0 over 967 commands; 70 more were held
# back by the execute-mode denylist (servers, daemons, comply) and are covered
# by the parse-mode gate instead.
#
# Necessarily a different number from documented-flags.baseline: it is measured
# over a smaller corpus, and it additionally catches missing-required-argument,
# which clap short-circuits past whenever it sees --help.
